sson_name", "content": "Sally and the Job Inquiry"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Writing a Cover Letter"}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "scholar > Leisure Time > Cell Phones Disturb the Peace"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 15}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange advice and suggestions in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present perfect continuous vs. Present perfect"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use these tenses  to express that an action that began in the past is still going on or has just finished. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You usually use the <span class=\"italic\">Present Perfect tense</span> to express that an action is completed or to emphasize the result. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Forms:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Regular verbs: form of <span class=\"italic\">have</span> + base form of verb + <span class=\"italic\">-ed</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Example: I have worked at the bakery for six years.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<br/>Irregular verbs: form of <span class=\"italic\">have</span> + past participle of irregular verbs"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Example: I have written a number of books in the last two years.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the <span class=\"italic\">Present Perfect Continuous</span> tense to emphasize the duration or continuity of an action."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Form:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Form of <span class=\"italic\">have</span> + <span class=\"italic\">been</span> + base form of verb +<span class=\"italic\"> -ing</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Example: We have been working for two hours!</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I have been attending Weston College as a journalism student since last year."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I have previously worked as an event coordinator and liaison officer at the Cambridge Community Center."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I have always maintained strong ties with the community."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Writing a Cover Letter"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A cover letter is a single-page letter that should be included in a job application.  It needs to be engaging and show the employer that you have the skills, education and experience to do the job."}, {"type": "text", "content": "There is certain information that you should include in a cover letter."}, {"type": "text", "content": "1. Put your name and contact details at the top of your cover letter. Ensure that your e-mail address sounds professional to create the right impression."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Also, include the name, position and contact details of the person you are writing to under your contact details. It is important to determine the name of person and not simply use, \u201cTo Whom It May Concern\u201d."}, {"type": "text", "content": "2. Explain which job you are applying for. For example: <span class=\"italic\">I am writing to apply for the advertised Entry-Level Journalist position</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "3. Your cover letter should include a summary of your education, skills and experience that match the job description. It needs to respond to all the essential requirements of the position as well as any additional information that may be desirable."}, {"type": "text", "content": "4. After listing your education, skills and experience, you need to explain why you are suited to the job. For example: <span class=\"italic\">My previous work as a liaison officer and interest in current affairs makes me ideally suited for this job.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "5. Your cover letter should finish by suggesting that the hiring manager review your r\u00e9sum\u00e9 as well as contact you about an interview. For example:  <span class=\"italic\">I have attached a copy of my r\u00e9sum\u00e9 for your consideration. I look forward to hearing from you about this application.</span>"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dynamic"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "always active or changing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I would like to develop my journalism skills in a fast-paced, dynamic environment."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le15ob08aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you would read in a cover letter."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to enhance"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to increase or improve"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This position provided the opportunity for me to enhance my written communication skills. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le15ob08aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tie"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a connection"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have always maintained strong ties with the community."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le15ob08aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "suited"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "right for, or appropriate for"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My interest in current affairs and related experience makes me ideally suited to this job."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le15ob08aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "consideration"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "careful thought; the act of thinking carefully about something you will make a decision about"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Thank you very much for your time and consideration."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le15ob08aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to interact"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to talk or do things with other people"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I interacted with a number of community groups."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le15ob08aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "work ethic"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a strong belief in the importance and value of work"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The job required a strong work ethic."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le15ob08aud07"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le15ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a 12 line dialogue between you and a friend."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Your friend asks you questions about what to include in a cover letter."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Tell your friend what to include and what to avoid."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Describe the structure of a cover letter."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Include the Present Perfect Continuous tense and Present Perfect tense like <span class=\"italic\">I have worked ...</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the dialogue aloud with a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write a dialogue about writing a cover letter."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use the Present Perfect Continuous tense and Present Perfect tense to explain events."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain what to include and not include in a cover letter."}]}]}